  "body": " The relationship between slopes of perpendicular lines    Two generic perpendicular lines, where one has slope .   the graph of two perpendicular lines, where one has a slope of m      Since the one slope is , we can draw a slope triangle with run  and rise  .   the previous graph with a slope triangle added; the rise is m and the run is 1      A congruent slope triangle can be drawn for the perpendicular line. It's legs have the same lengths, but in different positions, and one is negative.   the previous graph with the perpendicular line and its slope triangle added; the perpendicular line has a rise of -1 and a run of m which gives a slope of -1\/m      "
